================================================================================
Third-party data
================================================================================

No third-party code is distributed with this project. The iOS app links only
Apple frameworks, and the Python under pipeline/ and server/ is not distributed
to end users.

The project is *built from* three open geodata sources, each of which requires
attribution. The user-facing attribution is carried by the app itself, in each
licensor's own wording, at ios/Sources/AboutView.swift and asserted by
ios/Tests/AttributionTests.swift. Those strings are canonical — change them
there, not here. They are reproduced below so this file is complete on its own.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
OpenStreetMap — roads, street names and routing
Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0 — https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright

  © OpenStreetMap contributors
  Extracts processed by Geofabrik GmbH

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ESA WorldCover 10 m 2021 v200 — forest and green cover in the scenery scores
Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
https://esa-worldcover.org

  © ESA WorldCover project 2021 / Contains modified Copernicus Sentinel data
  (2021) processed by ESA WorldCover consortium

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Terrain Tiles (AWS Open Data, formerly Mapzen) — hills and valleys in the
scenery scores. An aggregate of national elevation products, each with its own
attribution; see https://registry.opendata.aws/terrain-tiles/ and
https://github.com/tilezen/joerd/blob/master/docs/attribution.md

  United States 3DEP (formerly NED) and global GMTED2010 and SRTM terrain data
  courtesy of the U.S. Geological Survey.

  Global ETOPO1 terrain data U.S. National Oceanic and Atmospheric
  Administration

  Canada terrain data contains information licensed under the Open Government
  Licence – Canada;

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Apple Maps, via MapKit — the basemap the routes are drawn on. MapKit renders
Apple's own attribution and legal link, so no string is owed here.

